      {
        "id": 98795,
        "name": "lynkfox",
        "username": "lynkfox",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lynkfox/{size}/1997_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-04-05T16:45:37.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>29 minatures, round it to 30, fully painted is entirely worth 150 bucks. Entirely. Even at chinese sweet shop paint jobs. Fully Painted minature lines, sch as HeroClix or others usually are 10-15 bucks for a booster of 5 mini's. Given that they're production costs are going to be a whooole lot less than &gt;G, 5 bucks a minature is not a bad price point at all.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Given that it will probably be unity and her bots as the next two goals, I can bet and expect 36 minatures, painted, for 150 dollars, less than 5 dollars a minature.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>That's... really good actually. Really good.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I'll still paint your minatures if you want, but not for that cheap :P</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>if you care, here is some photo's of some unfinished 40k work</p><p>http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v687/lynkfox/Warhammer/DSCF1843.jpg (base and weapon still had to be finished)</p><p>http://smg.photobucket.com/user/lynkfox/media/Warhammer/Skittari/DSC00182.jpg.html?sort=3&amp;o=11 (base wasn't even built, and still had to wash the black for detail)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>iw ould seriously paint them for money, but only semi serious. If you're going to pay someone to paint them, you'll get a much better deal and better end product out of someone else :P</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
