      {
        "id": 98796,
        "name": "Ironic",
        "username": "Ironic",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ironic/{size}/2171_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-04-05T21:34:44.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"lynkfox\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lynkfox/48/1997_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> lynkfox:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><span>29 minatures, round it to 30, fully painted is entirely worth 150 bucks. Entirely. Even at chinese sweet shop paint jobs. Fully Painted minature lines, sch as HeroClix or others usually are 10-15 bucks for a booster of 5 mini's. Given that they're production costs are going to be a whooole lot less than &gt;G, 5 bucks a minature is not a bad price point at all.&nbsp;Given that it will probably be unity and her bots as the next two goals, I can bet and expect 36 minatures, painted, for 150 dollars, less than 5 dollars a minature.&nbsp;That's… really good actually. Really good. <span></span></span></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p><span>Even better, since the first $60 of that is the cost of the minis themselves, so it's $90 for about 30 paint jobs. &nbsp;As painted minis go, this seems on point with Hero/Horror/Mage Knight Clix.</span></p>",
